      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The opposition's stance frequently rests on concerns about accountability, arguing that private schools receiving public funds may not be held to the same rigorous educational standards as public schools. Another key argument is that state aid should support a single, comprehensive public system rather than fragmenting it. While resistance to change is a factor, the core logical arguments focus on equitable funding and the duty of the state to provide a unified K-12 safety net.",
      "source": "target",
